    "time_horizon": "this-parliament",
    "confidence": "moderate",
    "plain": "This policy commits to implementing the Infected Blood Inquiry recommendations in full, including fair compensation for over 30,000 people who were harmed through NHS-administered contaminated blood \u2014 a major historic failure of due process and state accountability. Progress is real but victim groups have raised ongoing concerns about fairness and delays in the scheme's rollout.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether the compensation scheme will reach all eligible claimants fairly and in a timely way, given the Inquiry Chair's own criticism of 'unfair elements' and the uncertainty in the number of eligible claimants (government estimates range from 8,500 to 16,500 infected people, with up to 51,000 affected people potentially eligible).",
